# einheit-config v1
#
# Shipped factory defaults, read by `load factory` in the CLI. Install
# as /etc/einheit/s5/factory.conf — part of the image, NOT of the
# writable state directory, so a factory reset cannot be pointed at a
# file the operator edited.
#
# Format: one `<schema-path> <value>` line per setting; `#` comments and
# blank lines are ignored. Exactly what `save <name>` writes, so a
# known-good box can produce this file with `save` and a copy off the
# state directory.
#
# Absent from the image, `load factory` stages the EMPTY configuration
# instead, which on commit returns the box to its own power-on defaults.
#
# Factory reset from the CLI:
#     configure
#     load factory
#     show diff
#     commit
#
# This file is also what a factory-fresh box boots into: `--apply-boot`
# with no commit history applies it and records it as commit 1. That is
# not a convenience — every Linux switch port comes up administratively
# DOWN, so an unseeded box would ship forwarding nothing. The port lines
# below are what turn the switch on.
#
# lan1..lan4 are bridged into br0 by the fabric bootstrap (which is
# hardcoded, not config); lan5 is left routed as the uplink. Only
# settings the operator can change belong here.
#
# NOTE: no `poe.*` lines on purpose. The backend rejects any poe path
# when the I2C bus is unreadable, so a poe line here would turn a dead
# PoE bus into a box that cannot complete its first boot. The PSE
# controllers come up enabled in hardware; PoE is configured after boot.
#
# NOTE: no management addressing either, and that is an OPEN PRODUCT
# DECISION rather than an omission — how a factory-fresh S501 is first
# reached (console only, DHCP client on br0, or a fixed address) has not
# been decided. Watch out when adding it: `interfaces.<i>.dhcp true`
# takes precedence over `interfaces.<i>.address` in the backend and
# flushes it, so shipping `interfaces.br0.dhcp true` here would make an
# operator's later `set interfaces.br0.address` appear to do nothing
# until they also `delete interfaces.br0.dhcp`.

# NOTE: `stp.mode rstp` is deliberate and is the one line here that can
# stop a factory-fresh box from finishing its first boot — the backend
# rejects a spanning-tree commit on a box without mstpd rather than
# pretending loop protection is on. That is the trade we want: a shipped
# switch that melts the first time somebody patches two wall sockets
# together is worse than one that refuses to boot on an image missing a
# package its own factory defaults name. The image MUST ship mstpd +
# mstpctl (see deploy/README.md).

hostname einheit-s5
stp.mode rstp
ports.lan1.enabled true
ports.lan2.enabled true
ports.lan3.enabled true
ports.lan4.enabled true
ports.lan5.enabled true
